esentative Karianne Lisonbee, a fight centered on redistricting and data centers, and now faces Democrat Peter Crosby along with several minor-party candidates. Moore has raised about $2.5 million and holds $1.9 million on hand, while Crosby has raised roughly $60,000 with minimal cash remaining.\n\nA September poll sponsored by Crosby's campaign showed the race tied, and some local coverage echoed that framing, but the survey is partisan and the district's fundamentals remain heavily Republican. Prediction markets give Moore about a 95% chance of winning. The realistic range runs from a comfortable Moore win to a closer-than-expected margin if Democratic enthusiasm materializes.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0478, "margin": -11.61}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0598, "margin": -12.0}]}